@HostAddress = http://localhost:5100
@UserId = user-yarik-01
@LaptopId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@MouseId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### 1. List available products from Product Service (over HTTP)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

### 2. Use Case 1 (Command): Create a new Shopping Cart
# Automatically saves the returned cartId into Rider's global {{cartId}} variable!
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/carts
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{UserId}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("cartId", response.body.cartId);
%}

### 3. Use Case 2 (Command): Add 2 Laptops to Cart (reserves stock for 15 minutes over HTTP)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{LaptopId}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 4. Use Case 4 (Query): View Cart Contents and Total Value
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. View Event Sourcing Stream for the Cart
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/events
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Use Case 3 (Command): Remove 1 Laptop from Cart (releases 1 unit of stock lock over HTTP, 1 remains)
DELETE {{HostAddress}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{LaptopId}}?quantity=1
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}

### 7. Use Case 5 (Command): Checkout Cart (confirms cart & triggers Order Domain processing + notification)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/checkout
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 8. Order Domain (Query): Check User Orders
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/orders
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Order Domain (Query): Check User Notifications (+0.25 criterion)
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/orders/notifications
X-User-Id: {{UserId}}
Accept: application/json
